# Exocortex — Round 7 Review (Wave 2 boundary)

**Status:** CLOSED (2026-09-02). Scope: the Wave 2 boundary review of
the 2026-09-02 run's three commits — D1 iceberg (`78518a8`), D1 delta
(`3e9453e`), D17 (`04e8adc`) — plus the shared-core extraction
(`exocortex-adapter-table`) they introduced. Method: adversarial read
of the new surface against the formats' specifications (Iceberg v1/v2,
Delta classic protocol, Fellegi-Sunter) and this repo's invariants,
with every accepted finding verified against the source before
inclusion. Findings landed through the master-plan lifecycle in the
same commits as their fixes.

## Baseline

`04e8adc` (2026-09-02). New hand-authored surface reviewed:
`crates/exocortex-adapter-iceberg` (lib, bin, tests),
`crates/exocortex-adapter-delta` (lib, bin, tests),
`crates/exocortex-entity-resolution` (lib, bin, tests),
`crates/exocortex-adapter-table` (lib), the `exocortex-adapter-parquet`
slim-down, the ADAPTER_CONTRACT gate rows + bijection skip, and the
PUBLISHING.md dependency records.

## Findings

### R7-1 — Iceberg manifest paths are not URI-decoded (blocker)

Iceberg writers commonly URI-encode paths in manifests and metadata
(spaces as `%20`, per the spec's file:// path conventions). The
iceberg adapter's `resolve_path` treated them literally, so a real
table whose data paths contain a space would fail to open — and fail
during the row read, after the scan had already claimed the file set.
The Delta adapter decoded correctly; the two flavors disagreed, which
is exactly the divergence class the shared crate exists to prevent.

**Fix:** `percent_decode` moved to `exocortex-adapter-table` as the
one implementation; both flavors' path resolution decodes through it.
Regression: `percent_escaped_paths_decode` (delta, pre-existing) and a
new iceberg fixture whose manifest `file_path` carries `%20`, proving
the overlay path resolves and rows read.

### R7-2 — The Avro value decoder had no Union arm (blocker, latent)

`apache_avro::from_avro_datum` with no reader schema returns
`Value::Union(index, inner)` for union-typed fields. The iceberg
adapter's `avro_value_to_json` matched every concrete variant and
fell back to `format!("{other:?}")` — a non-null union would silently
decode to a Debug-string placeholder instead of its value. No shipped
path reads a union field today (`snapshot_id` is never consulted), so
nothing was yet wrong in behavior — but a decoder with a
silent-corruption shape is a defect waiting for its first caller.

**Fix:** a `Union(_, inner)` arm that unwraps to the inner value.
Regression: a v1 manifest entry whose `snapshot_id` union is the LONG
branch (non-null), asserted to decode as a number via the public
record-field path.

### R7-3 — The ER harness could not pin thresholds at classification time (advisory)

`exocortex-er classify` used the calibrated thresholds with no
override. An operator iterating on the labelled set (the harness's
whole workflow: measure, adjust, re-classify) had to accept the
calibration as-is or edit code. Advisory, not behavioral: calibration
remains the default and remains printed by `evaluate`.

**Fix:** `--accept` / `--review` optional overrides on `classify`.
Regression: harness test classifying with an explicit `--review` low
enough to surface review-band pairs.

## Verified-safe notes (recorded so they are not re-derived)

- The iceberg OCF framing reader's negative map-block-count handling
  consumes the block-size long AND the pairs (verified against the
  Avro spec's container format); block payloads are sliced by the
  declared size, never length-prefixed again; sync markers are
  validated per block.
- The delta checkpoint multi-part completeness check derives the
  expected total from each part's own filename, so a deleted part
  fails closed without trusting `_last_checkpoint`.
- Delta's `_last_checkpoint` is a hint only; a v2-checkpoint pointer
  (sidecar files) fails closed rather than replaying a stale state.
- Fellegi-Sunter thresholds are calibrated from the labelled scores
  (midpoint boundary, 3/4 toward each mean); a feature with
  match-only evidence refuses estimation; both classes are required.
- The adapter-contract gate's bijection skip now names `table` with
  the same rationale `sdk` has carried (a library the adapters link,
  not a source); the negative fixture still rejects unclaimed adapter
  crates.

## Verdict

Changes requested at baseline; both blockers and the advisory landed
with fail-without-it regressions in the same commits, and the master
plan's R7 rows carry the closing evidence. Wave 2's
locally-satisfiable rows (D21, D18, D13, PX4, D1, D17) are closed;
D19 parks on owner credentials. The run proceeded to Wave 3.
